WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.101 --> 00:00:09.440
Patrick climbed onto the team bus on Friday to go to the game at West Middle School, home of the Bandits.

2
00:00:09.441 --> 00:00:14.104
He took a seat in the front and opened his math book.

3
00:00:14.105 --> 00:00:21.620
Dell slid in beside him and laughed when he saw the book. "You're doing math homework before the game?"

4
00:00:21.621 --> 00:00:25.363
"My last quiz pulled my grade down," mumbled Patrick.

5
00:00:25.364 --> 00:00:28.950
He was embarrassed to admit how poorly he was doing in math.

6
00:00:28.951 --> 00:00:35.188
He quickly closed the book. "But it's not a big deal. Let's talk baseball."

7
00:00:35.189 --> 00:00:41.600
At the ballpark Patrick carried his equipment bag to the dugout.

8
00:00:41.601 --> 00:00:45.852
He probably wouldn't need his catcher's equipment—unless Mickey got hurt.

9
00:00:45.853 --> 00:00:50.102
Patrick shook his head. He wanted the starting catcher spot.

10
00:00:50.103 --> 00:00:58.325
But he wanted to win it fairly, not because someone else was injured. He ran out to left field to warm up.

11
00:00:58.326 --> 00:01:04.331
Before the fifth inning, Patrick caught three flies and fielded some easy grounders.

12
00:01:04.332 --> 00:01:10.751
His playing was nothing spectacular, but it was nice to hear his father cheering, even from a distance.

13
00:01:10.752 --> 00:01:15.398
Now it was the top of the sixth inning, and Patrick was up to bat.

14
00:01:15.399 --> 00:01:20.570
He flexed his fingers inside his batting gloves, trying to loosen up.

15
00:01:20.571 --> 00:01:26.251
He had popped out his first time at bat, and he got tagged out at first base on his second time at bat.

16
00:01:26.252 --> 00:01:31.043
He faced the pitcher again, every fiber in his body wanting a hit.

17
00:01:31.044 --> 00:01:34.927
His hands tightened on the bat. His muscles tensed.

18
00:01:34.928 --> 00:01:36.133
Crack!

19
00:01:36.134 --> 00:01:40.210
The ball popped over the right field stands. Foul.

20
00:01:40.211 --> 00:01:46.375
Patrick stepped out from the batter's box and imagined that he was the opposing catcher crouched behind home plate.

21
00:01:46.376 --> 00:01:54.932
As a catcher, Patrick would think, "This batter is trying too hard. He's tense. He'll swing at the next one."

22
00:01:54.933 --> 00:02:02.757
Patrick stepped back into the box, carefully positioned his feet, and raised the bat.

23
00:02:02.758 --> 00:02:08.279
The pitch was outside the plate, and he let it go, without swinging.

24
00:02:08.280 --> 00:02:10.632
"Ball!" said the umpire.

25
00:02:10.633 --> 00:02:13.119
"Nice job," he told himself.

26
00:02:13.120 --> 00:02:15.675
The next pitch was high.

27
00:02:15.676 --> 00:02:18.839
Patrick didn't swing again—another ball.

28
00:02:18.840 --> 00:02:24.738
Patrick hid his grin. "Now the pitcher will try to whiz the ball past me," he thought.

29
00:02:24.739 --> 00:02:27.152
Fastball.

30
00:02:27.154 --> 00:02:28.587
Crack!

31
00:02:28.588 --> 00:02:33.069
The bat connected and Patrick ran.

32
00:02:33.070 --> 00:02:38.335
He rounded first base, glancing at Coach, who gave him the signal to go.

33
00:02:38.336 --> 00:02:44.274
Patrick's legs churned and then he slid into second base.

34
00:02:44.274 --> 00:02:47.234
"Safe!" called the umpire.

35
00:02:47.235 --> 00:02:54.917
Patrick brushed off his pants as the crowd cheered. "A double," he thought. "Yes!"

36
00:02:54.918 --> 00:02:57.707
Mickey was up next.

37
00:02:57.708 --> 00:03:02.647
Patrick inched toward third base, his eyes on Daniel, the third-base coach.

38
00:03:02.648 --> 00:03:07.892
His adrenaline pumped. He might get to home, if he was fast enough.

39
00:03:07.893 --> 00:03:14.307
He didn't have to worry about it. Mickey slammed the ball over the fence. Homerun!

40
00:03:14.308 --> 00:03:16.709
The score was 4-4.

41
00:03:16.710 --> 00:03:24.472
The next Dragon hitter struck out, giving the team three outs. Patrick ran back to left field.

42
00:03:24.473 --> 00:03:27.464
"Batter up!" called the umpire.

43
00:03:27.465 --> 00:03:34.443
From his spot in left field, Patrick couldn't see the other fielders, and Dell looked like a flagpole on the mound.

44
00:03:34.444 --> 00:03:38.630
He couldn't read the signal Mickey put down for the pitch.

45
00:03:38.631 --> 00:03:43.603
Crack! A hard grounder zinged past Gene on third base.

46
00:03:43.604 --> 00:03:50.785
Patrick ran forward and scooped it up. He shot the ball to first.

47
00:03:50.786 --> 00:03:54.448
As soon as it left his hand, he knew it was high.

48
00:03:54.449 --> 00:03:59.270
If the ball went over Buck's head, the Bandits runner might even get a double.

49
00:03:59.271 --> 00:04:04.771
Buck leaped up and brought down the ball. The runner was safe on first.

50
00:04:04.772 --> 00:04:07.929
"Nice catch, Buck!" yelled Mr. Deboe.

51
00:04:07.930 --> 00:04:14.429
Patrick scuffed the grass with his toe. Buck had saved him on that one.

52
00:04:14.430 --> 00:04:18.766
Patrick wished he was playing where he belonged, behind home plate.

53
00:04:18.767 --> 00:04:20.861
When he was catching, he didn't—

54
00:04:20.862 --> 00:04:22.762
Crack!

55
00:04:22.763 --> 00:04:31.488
Too late Patrick realized the next batter had gotten a hit. Patrick spotted the fly ball coming toward him and ran.

56
00:04:31.489 --> 00:04:42.625
"Faster!" he told himself. He dove as the ball came down. It nicked the tip of his glove and bounced off.

57
00:04:42.626 --> 00:04:48.640
Patrick scrambled to his feet, picked up the ball, and rocketed it to second.

58
00:04:48.641 --> 00:04:52.274
The umpire spread his arms. "Safe!"

59
00:04:52.275 --> 00:04:54.885
"Good try!" somebody yelled.

60
00:04:54.886 --> 00:04:59.881
"Not good enough," Patrick thought as he jogged back to position.

61
00:04:59.882 --> 00:05:09.709
The next batter hit a double and brought one runner in. The Bandits fans went wild.

62
00:05:09.710 --> 00:05:13.538
After seven innings the Dragons lost, 5-4.

63
00:05:13.539 --> 00:05:15.445
Coach gathered the team.

64
00:05:15.446 --> 00:05:21.774
"You fought hard. We won't win every game, but teamwork will carry us to the championship.

65
00:05:21.775 --> 00:05:25.034
Everybody has to give all they've got."

66
00:05:25.035 --> 00:05:32.290
"This loss is my fault," thought Patrick. He'd been moping about playing left field instead of watching the batter.

67
00:05:32.291 --> 00:05:36.255
His head wasn't in the game, and it had cost the team.

68
00:05:36.256 --> 00:05:40.947
The players started heading for the parking lot.

69
00:05:40.948 --> 00:05:45.365
"Look!" said Dell. "It's got a tail now!"

70
00:05:45.366 --> 00:05:54.423
Patrick glanced at the van. Dell was right. The van now had a tail—and it was wagging! Patrick groaned.

71
00:05:54.424 --> 00:05:59.184
This had to be what Dad and Daniel were working on in the garage last weekend.

72
00:05:59.185 --> 00:06:05.175
"Hey, Patrick," said Buck. "Can I look inside the van? Sheila said it's really cool."

73
00:06:05.176 --> 00:06:07.254
"Me too," said Gene.

74
00:06:07.255 --> 00:06:11.156
Patrick shrugged. "Sure. It's just a van."

75
00:06:11.157 --> 00:06:16.655
"Our dog, Bitsy, loved it!" said Sheila. "It's like a doggie spa."

76
00:06:16.656 --> 00:06:22.247
Everyone wanted to see it, so Patrick led both baseball teams to the Doggie Express van.

77
00:06:22.248 --> 00:06:28.809
Kids gathered around as his mother swung open the back doors. Patrick shook his head.

78
00:06:28.810 --> 00:06:33.625
Why was everyone so excited? It wasn’t like his mom drove an ice cream truck.

79
00:06:33.626 --> 00:06:39.296
Mrs. Deboe showed off the folding tables, self-heating tub, and little doggie mirrors.

80
00:06:39.297 --> 00:06:43.634
"My beagle would love this!" said the Bandits pitcher.

81
00:06:43.635 --> 00:06:50.307
Somebody else laughed. "My boxer wouldn't like it. He hates water more than trips to the vet."

82
00:06:50.308 --> 00:06:57.109
The kids laughed and talked about their dogs as they walked off to find their rides or get back on a bus.

83
00:06:57.110 --> 00:07:04.657
Daniel and Mr. Deboe huddled to talk about the game while Patrick's mom put away stuff in the van.

84
00:07:04.658 --> 00:07:07.280
A few kids stood near Patrick.

85
00:07:07.281 --> 00:07:10.867
"What kind of dog do you have, Mickey?" asked Sheila.

86
00:07:10.868 --> 00:07:16.524
"You've probably never seen one," said Mickey. "Ratty's an Irish wolfhound."

87
00:07:16.525 --> 00:07:20.443
"Hey! Our dog, Bitsy, is a wolfhound!" said Buck.

88
00:07:20.444 --> 00:07:24.397
Mickey grinned. "We should get them together at the dog park."

89
00:07:24.398 --> 00:07:28.761
"A playdate for dogs!" Buck laughed. "Let's do it!"

90
00:07:28.762 --> 00:07:32.028
"What kind of dog do you have, Patrick?" asked Mickey.

91
00:07:32.029 --> 00:07:35.764
"Daniel has a mutt. I have a cat," muttered Patrick.

92
00:07:35.765 --> 00:07:38.467
"Oh, cats are cool," said Mickey.

93
00:07:38.468 --> 00:07:41.456
"Yep." Patrick stared down at the ground.

94
00:07:41.458 --> 00:07:52.528
For once he couldn't wait for his mother to start up that dumb doggy van—and take him home.

